> Module Unemployment

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Unemployment compensation (Form 1099-G; Schedule 1 line 7, Form 1040 line 8)

Direct File module `unemployment.xml`
(`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/unemployment.xml`,
"DF" below), scope.md section 3.4, issue #21. Tests:
`catala/tests/test_unemployment.catala_en`. Oracle comparison:
`make difftest SCOPE=unemployment`.

Inputs are complete (`catala/CONVENTIONS.md` section 3): an empty box of a
Form 1099-G is an explicit `$0`. This module feeds three things to the Form
1040 scope (#14), listed in the PR body: `unemployment_compensation` (slot
`unemployment_compensation`, Schedule 1 line 7 and then 1040 line 8),
`form_1099g_federal_tax_withheld` (part of the slot `other_1099_withholding`,
1040 line 25b), and `unsupported` (return-level knockout aggregation, #38).

## Statute and form

Unemployment compensation is gross income. 26 U.S.C. § 85 is not among the
files in `sources/statute/`, so the form and its instructions are the cited
source. Schedule 1 (Form 1040) 2024, `sources/forms-instructions/f1040s1--2024.pdf`
p 1, line 7: "Unemployment compensation". Instructions for Form 1040 2024,
`sources/forms-instructions/i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 85, "Line 7, Unemployment
Compensation": "You should receive a Form 1099-G showing in box 1 the total
unemployment compensation paid to you in 2024. Report this amount on line 7."
and "If you received an overpayment of unemployment compensation in 2024 and
you repaid any of it in 2024, subtract the amount you repaid from the total
amount you received. Enter the result on line 7. Also enter "Repaid" and the
amount you repaid on the dotted line next to line 7. If, in 2024, you repaid
more than $3,000 of unemployment compensation you included in gross income in
an earlier year, see Repayments in Pub. 525."

The $3,000 is the threshold of 26 U.S.C. § 1341(a)(3)
(`sources/statute/irc-1341.html`): relief under the claim-of-right rule applies
"if the amount of such deduction exceeds $3,000". Direct File does not
compute the § 1341 computation; it refuses the filer (knockout below).
`P.claim_of_right_threshold` holds the figure.

Rounding. The instruction says to subtract the repayment from the amount
received and enter the result. Direct File computes a net amount for each form
without rounding, adds the nets, and rounds the sum once
(`/unemploymentCompensation = Round(CollectionSum(netUnemploymentComp))`). The
federal tax withheld of each form is rounded per form (a per-item `Round`, the
pattern of scope.md section 3.1; Q-R1 in `CONVENTIONS.md`).

## One Form 1099-G

DF collection `/form1099Gs`. The `Writable` children are fields of
`Form1099G`; the derived children are outputs of the scope `Form1099GFacts`.
Payer name, TINs, state ID and the "has a 1099" flag change no tax result and
are not modelled.

```catala-metadata
## One entry of DF `/form1099Gs`: the boxes of a Form 1099-G the tax depends on.
declaration structure Form1099G:
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/filer (CollectionItem of /filers)
  data filer content Types.FilerRole
  # 1099-G box 1. DF: /form1099Gs/*/amount
  data amount content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/writableAmountPaidBackForBenefitsInTaxYear: repayment, in
  # the tax year, of benefits received in the tax year.
  data writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/writableAmountPaidBackForBenefitsBeforeTaxYear:
  # repayment, in the tax year, of benefits received in an earlier year.
  data writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year content money
  # 1099-G box 4. DF: /form1099Gs/*/writableFederalTaxWithheld
  data writable_federal_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/writableState: true when the filer chose
  # `differentState` from /incomeFormStateOptions (`sameState` or no answer:
  # false).
  data state_is_different_state content boolean
```

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Form1099GFacts:
  input form content Form1099G
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/amountPaidBackForBenefitsInTaxYear
  output amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/netUnemploymentComp
  output net_unemployment_comp content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/amountPaidBackForBenefitsBeforeTaxYear
  output amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/federalTaxWithheld
  output federal_tax_withheld content money
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/hasKnockoutUnemploymentCompensationInDifferentState
  output has_knockout_unemployment_compensation_in_different_state condition
```

```catala
scope Form1099GFacts:
  # DF-BUG(candidate): DF caps the repayment at box 1 ("a stopgap to prevent the
  # amount being paid back from being greater than the amount being paid",
  # unemployment.xml, TODO issue 4962). The 1040 instructions have no cap: a
  # repayment above box 1 would make line 7 negative. The cap is kept as it matches the issue #21 case and
  # only bites on inconsistent input (a same-year repayment above box 1);
  # the instruction would give a negative line 7.
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/amountPaidBackForBenefitsInTaxYear
  definition amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year equals
    Money.min of
      form.writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year, form.amount

  # "subtract the amount you repaid from the total amount you received"
  # (i1040gi--2024.pdf p 85). Not rounded here: DF rounds the sum.
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/netUnemploymentComp
  definition net_unemployment_comp equals
    form.amount - amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year

  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/amountPaidBackForBenefitsBeforeTaxYear
  definition amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year equals
    form.writable_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year

  # Box 4, rounded to the whole dollar per form. Feeds Form 1040 line 25b
  # (taxCalculations.xml /form1099Withholding).
  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/federalTaxWithheld
  definition federal_tax_withheld equals
    R.round_dollar of form.writable_federal_tax_withheld

  # DF: /form1099Gs/*/hasKnockoutUnemploymentCompensationInDifferentState
  rule has_knockout_unemployment_compensation_in_different_state
    under condition form.state_is_different_state
    consequence fulfilled
```

## All Forms 1099-G: Schedule 1 line 7 and line 25b

```catala-metadata
declaration scope Unemployment:
  # DF: /form1099Gs (Writable collection)
  input form_1099gs content list of Form1099G

  internal facts content list of Form1099GFacts

  # DF: /unemploymentCompensation (Schedule 1 line 7; downstream of
  # income.xml /otherIncome, Form 1040 line 8)
  output unemployment_compensation content money
  # DF: /unemploymentCompRepaidAmt (the "Repaid" amount next to line 7)
  output unemployment_comp_repaid_amt content money
  # DF: /receivedUnemploymentCompensation
  output received_unemployment_compensation condition
  # DF: /xmlHasRepaidUnemploymentCompensation (received and repaid > $0)
  output has_repaid_unemployment_compensation condition
  # DF: /totalAmountPaidBackForBenefitsBeforeTaxYear
  output total_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year content money
  # Sum of /form1099Gs/*/federalTaxWithheld, the 1099-G term of DF
  # taxCalculations.xml /form1099Withholding (Form 1040 line 25b).
  output form_1099g_federal_tax_withheld content money

  # Knockouts (catala/CONVENTIONS.md section 6).
  # DF: /flowKnockout1099GRepayTooHigh
  output ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high condition
  # DF: /flowKnockoutUnemploymentCompensationUnsupportedState
  output ko_flow_knockout_unemployment_compensation_unsupported_state condition
  # All knockouts of this scope (flow.xml /flowIsKnockedOut).
  output unsupported condition
```

```catala
scope Unemployment:
  definition facts equals
    map each f among form_1099gs to (output of Form1099GFacts with { -- form: f })

  # The nets are added with cents and only the total is rounded, as the 1040
  # instructions say (i1040gi--2024.pdf p 23); no per-form rounding here.
  # DF: /unemploymentCompensation
  definition unemployment_compensation equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.net_unemployment_comp))

  # DF: /unemploymentCompRepaidAmt
  definition unemployment_comp_repaid_amt equals
    R.round_dollar of
      (Money.sum of
        (map each f among facts to
          f.amount_paid_back_for_benefits_in_tax_year))

  # True when some form shows a box 1 above $0.
  # DF: /receivedUnemploymentCompensation
  rule received_unemployment_compensation
    under condition exists f among form_1099gs such that f.amount > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /xmlHasRepaidUnemploymentCompensation
  rule has_repaid_unemployment_compensation
    under condition
      received_unemployment_compensation and unemployment_comp_repaid_amt > $0
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /totalAmountPaidBackForBenefitsBeforeTaxYear
  definition total_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year equals
    Money.sum of
      (map each f among facts to
        f.amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year)

  # Sum of the per-form rounded box 4 amounts, no outer rounding (the DF
  # `Add` in /form1099Withholding has none).
  # DF: taxCalculations.xml /form1099Withholding, CollectionSum of
  # /form1099Gs/*/federalTaxWithheld
  definition form_1099g_federal_tax_withheld equals
    Money.sum of (map each f among facts to f.federal_tax_withheld)
```

## Knockouts

scope.md section 3.4: "Repayment of prior-year benefits above 3,000 is a
knockout." The instructions send such a filer to Pub. 525 (§ 1341 relief), which
Direct File does not compute. A filer who received 1099-G income from a state
other than the filer's own state is also refused.

```catala
scope Unemployment:
  # The repayments of all forms are added; the test is strictly "greater than"
  # $3,000 (IRC 1341(a)(3): "exceeds $3,000"). The in-year repayment of
  # this-year benefits (above) is not part of the test.
  # DF: /flowKnockout1099GRepayTooHigh (maximumRepaymentUnemploymentCompensation
  # is $3,000, here P.claim_of_right_threshold)
  rule ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
    under condition
      total_amount_paid_back_for_benefits_before_tax_year
        > P.claim_of_right_threshold
    consequence fulfilled

  # DF: /flowKnockoutUnemploymentCompensationUnsupportedState
  rule ko_flow_knockout_unemployment_compensation_unsupported_state
    under condition
      exists f among facts such that
        f.has_knockout_unemployment_compensation_in_different_state
    consequence fulfilled

  # The two DF knockouts of this module in flow.xml /flowIsKnockedOut.
  rule unsupported under condition
    ko_flow_knockout1099_g_repay_too_high
    or ko_flow_knockout_unemployment_compensation_unsupported_state
  consequence fulfilled
```
